{number: 133}
{title: Let the Lower Lights Be Burning}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Brightly beams our Father's mercy
From His [Eb] lighthouse ever-[Bb] more,
But to us He gives the keeping
Of the [F7] lights along the [Bb] shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb] Let the lower lights be burning!
Send a [Eb] gleam across the [Bb] wave!
Some poor fainting, struggling seaman
You may [F7] rescue, you may [Bb] save.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Dark the night of sin has settled,
Loud the [Eb] angry billows [Bb] roar;
Eager eyes are watching, longing,
For the [F7] lights along the [Bb] shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] Trim your feeble lamp, my brother;
Some poor [Eb] sailor, tempest-[Bb] tossed,
Trying now to make the harbor,
In the [F7] darkness may be [Bb] lost.
{end_of_verse}
